# My everyday loaf based on morph

starter:
  ap_flour
  water
  hydration = 100%

leaven:
  starter
  bread_flour = 10 * starter
  cold_water
  hydration = 100%

grain:
  prairie_gold
  hard_red
  barley = 5%
  # spelt = 5%  # out of spelt
  wheat_germ = 5%
  buckwheat = 5%

dry:
  grain
  vwg = 3%
  potato_flakes = 5%
  yeast = 0.5%
  salt = 1.8%

wet:
  cold_water
  flourless_starter = 10%
  ascorbic_acid_1p = 50ppm * 100 * grain
  leaven = 40%
  olive_oil = 5%
  honey = 5%
  yogurt = 5%

dough:
  wet
  dry
  hydration = 70%
  # 200g/L of flour
  # total_flour = 660g # 13 inch
  # total_flour = 500g # 9 inch
  total = 1086g

/*
July 27, 2026

Changes
- Only 9g of starter remaining!
- Mix a larger than needed leaven and use the rest for starter
- replace spelt with toasted wheat germ
- increase total by 100g for old dough

Zoji pan weighs 773g. KA pan weighs 725g.

Starter is 8 days old.

Mixed the leaven about 16:20 left on the counter. Initial T is 76.4.

Leaven pH = 3.67 at 7:25 dt is 75F. It rose to the top of the 500ml
container and had started to fall.

I started about 7:20

Used the KA for mixing. Mixed about 7:34. Stopped after 2 minutes;
it cleaned the bowl. DT after mixing is 72F. RT is 76F. 

30 minute rest in fridge.

Kneaded 7 minutes in KA. It was cleaning the bowl and looking great.

Into the cambro and the fridge at 8:20. S&F every 30 minutes.

Into the pan at 9:40. Left on the counter at 76F.

100g of dough into fridge.

Baked at 12:20 for 45 minutes at 350F lid off.

I added 100ml of water to the pan before preheating the oven.

I forgot about it and let it rise too far. It turned out great but
hippy. 

Super soft and delicious. Less sour than the last one.

*/

